To create a Chrome extension that saves the contents of the current webpage, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. **Set up your project structure**: Create a new directory for your extension and inside it, create two files: `manifest.json` and `content.js`.

2. **Create the manifest file** (`manifest.json`): This file contains metadata about your extension and specifies its permissions and background scripts.

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Save Page Content",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Saves the content of the current webpage.",
  "permissions": [
    "activeTab",
    "storage"
  ],
  "background": {
    "service_worker": "background.js"
  },
  "action": {
    "default_popup": "popup.html",
    "default_icon": {
      "16": "icons/icon16.png",
      "48": "icons/icon48.png",
      "128": "icons/icon128.png"
    }
  }
}
```

3. **Create the popup HTML** (`popup.html`): This is where users will interact with your extension. It should include a button to trigger saving the page content.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Save Page Content</title>
  <style>
    body { width: 200px; padding: 10px; }
    button { display: block; margin-top: 10px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Save Page Content</h1>
  <button id="saveButton">Save Current Page</button>
  <script src="popup.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

4. **Create the popup script** (`popup.js`): This script handles the logic when the user clicks the save button.

```javascript
document.getElementById('saveButton').addEventListener('click', () => {
  chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }, (tabs) => {
    const tab = tabs[0];
    if (tab && tab.id) {
      chrome.scripting.executeScript({
        target: { tabId: tab.id },
        function: savePageContent
      });
    }
  });
});

function savePageContent() {
  // Get the entire document as text
  const content = document.documentElement.outerHTML;

  // Save the content using local storage or another method
  localStorage.setItem('savedPageContent', content);

  alert('Page content saved!');
}
```

5. **Load your extension into Chrome**: Go to `chrome://extensions/`, enable Developer Mode, click on "Load unpacked", select your extension's folder, and load it.

